2776 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1897 0 R
/E (The Kingdom of God is God's sovereign rule over all creation. It is not limited by geography. It is not confined to a church building. It is not identified with one nation or culture. Wherever God's will is joyfully obeyed, His Kingdom is present. Jesus came to announce that God's Kingdom had drawn near. He invites every person to leave the kingdom of self and enter the Kingdom of God through faith in Him.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2777 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1897 0 R
/T (2. Two Kingdoms)
/E (2. Two Kingdoms)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2778 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1897 0 R
/E (Every person lives under one of two kingdoms. The kingdom of self says: "My will be done." "My desires come first." "My life belongs to me.")
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2779 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1897 0 R
/E (The Kingdom of God says: "Your will be done." "My life belongs to Christ." "I live for His glory." The greatest battle of the Christian life is not between people. It is between these two kingdoms. Every day we choose which kingdom will govern our hearts.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
