2989 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1905 0 R
/E (The cross was more than a symbol. It represented complete obedience to the Father. When Jesus tells us to take up our cross daily, He invites us into the same life of obedience. Sometimes obedience requires sacrifice. Sometimes it requires patience. Sometimes forgiveness. Sometimes courage. Sometimes letting go of what we want so we can embrace what God desires. The cross reminds us that following Jesus costs something. But it also reminds us that nothing we surrender to Christ is ever lost in His Kingdom.)
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
