3115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1910 0 R
/E (To abide means to remain, dwell, continue, or stay closely connected. Abiding in Christ is not visiting Him occasionally. It is making Him the center of our daily lives. It means trusting Him in every circumstance. Listening to His voice through His Word. Speaking with Him in prayer. Walking in obedience. Depending upon His grace every day. Abiding is not an activity we perform once. It is the atmosphere in which a disciple lives.)
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
