/P 1917 0 R
/T (1. What Is the Fruit of the Spirit?)
/E (1. What Is the Fruit of the Spirit?)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
3271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1917 0 R
/E (Notice that Paul says "fruit," not "fruits." The fruit of the Spirit is one beautiful picture of Christ's character expressed in many ways. Love...Joy... Peace... Patience... Kindness... Goodness... Faithfulness... Gentleness...Self-control... These qualities describe the life of Jesus Himself. As we walk with Him, His character begins to shape ours. Christian maturity is becoming more like Christ.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
3272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1917 0 R
/T (2. Fruit Grows Naturally)
/E (2. Fruit Grows Naturally)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
3273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1917 0 R
/E (No tree struggles to produce fruit. It simply remains rooted, receives nourishment, and grows. The same is true for believers. When we abide in Christ... pray... study His Word... walk in obedience... and depend upon the Holy Spirit... our lives begin to change. Sometimes the growth is slow. Sometimes we hardly notice it. Yet God is faithfully at work. Spiritual growth is often gradual, but it is always meaningful.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
