4059 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1956 0 R
/T (1. What Does It Mean to Glorify God?)
/E (1. What Does It Mean to Glorify God?)
/Pg 106 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
4060 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1956 0 R
/E (To glorify God means to honor Him, reflect His character, and acknowledge His greatness in everything we do. We cannot add to God's glory, for He is already infinitely glorious. But we can live in ways that reveal His goodness, wisdom, holiness, and love. Jesus perfectly glorified the Father through His obedience, humility, compassion, and sacrifice. As we become more like Christ, our lives also become a testimony to God's glory. Every act of faith, every word of truth, and every expression of love can point others to Him.)
/Pg 106 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
